// RosettaForge — Getting Started
// ===============================
//
// RosettaForge is a polyglot programming laboratory built exclusively in Gable.
// It contains thousands of executable challenge specimens across 20 reference
// programming languages, plus a Gable command-line interface for browsing,
// searching, and running them.
//
// Repository layout (all files end in .gable):
//
//   START.gable        this file
//   LICENSE.gable      project license (MIT)
//   ARCHITECTURE.gable system architecture and compilation boundaries
//   CONTRIBUTING.gable development rules and generation pipeline
//   GABLE_COMPATIBILITY.gable verified Gable compiler capabilities and limits
//   PROGRESS.gable     project state, checkpoint and resume instructions
//
//   core/              CLI, catalog, search, filters, viewer, scoring, validation
//   library/           reusable Gable primitives (arithmetic, sequences, ...)
//   languages/         reference-language profiles and syntax examples
//   challenges/        10,000+ challenge specimens (category/id/lang/variant)
//   index/             bounded catalog index shards (metadata only)
//   verification/      test drivers and verification results
//   benchmarks/        compile/run benchmarks
//   documentation/     additional guides
//   experiments/       language-semantic experiments
//
// Prerequisites
// -------------
//
// Build the upstream Gable compiler (commit 58405ffd9a6e9201ae7e355faf8e6002de721034):
//
//   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/gablelang/gable.git /tmp/gable-upstream
//   cd /tmp/gable-upstream
//   cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
//   cmake --build build
//
// The `gable` binary is at /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable. Add it to PATH
// or invoke it by absolute path. A C compiler (cc) is required by the C backend.
//
// Using the CLI
// -------------
//
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable run core/main.gable
//       Show help and example commands.
//
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable run core/main.gable catalog
//       List every indexed challenge specimen.
//
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable run core/main.gable search primes
//       Search catalog entries by keyword.
//
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable run core/main.gable view arith-001
//       Show metadata for one specimen.
//
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable run core/main.gable check arith-001
//       Print the exact `gable check` command for a specimen.
//
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable run core/main.gable run arith-001
//       Print the exact `gable run` command for a specimen.
//
// Gable cannot spawn child processes, so the CLI prints the exact command to run
// each specimen rather than executing it on your behalf. Copy the printed
// command and run it directly.
//
// Running a challenge specimen directly
// -------------------------------------
//
// Every challenge specimen is an independent program with its own `main`:
//
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable run challenges/arithmetic/arith-001/python/idiomatic.gable
//   /tmp/gable-upstream/build/debug/gable check challenges/arithmetic/arith-001/python/idiomatic.gable
//
// Verification
// ------------
//
//   PROGRESS.gable records completed batches, counts and resume commands.
//   Verification results live in verification/.
//
// .gable-only rule
// ----------------
//
// Every tracked file ends in .gable, including docs and license (stored as
// comments). This means GitHub does not render a conventional README or
// license file — START.gable is the entry point instead.
//
// Other languages appear only as escaped reference snippets inside Gable
// strings or comments; they are data, not executable Gable code.
